{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: one P2 in the complete three-subject R3 revision22 design at exact 55e41dfcdd71af5ce2c4548d45bca80236ad1f3e. Primary d5b69058 first, corrections de309a16 and facts 18038dba also examined. This is evidence-only ordinary design review under consolidated origin4a1c97f2 and producer promise14b22b97; no implementation closure or source acceptance.\n\nP2 — bound or partition the attempts admitted into one save. Main8027 limits cut.attempts to eight. New8077/8946 admits a further root-changing intend while a save is open and no cut is frozen, opens no separate save, and promises that the open save's cut names its attempt. With a running task, ready registration, valid grant, sufficient configured entry/byte/other capacity and an unfrozen cut, the first intend opens S and eight further distinct first-attempt intendes meet that same admission rule. S is promised nine members but can encode eight. The successor at8079/8949 and8395–8405 is a refused save's retry, at most three for the same attempt set; it supplies no successful partition continuation. This is an abstract contradiction among declared admission and closure clauses, not protocol simulation or evidence that nine commands ran. Adopted C2e354 section6:1317–1319 serializes mutations and forbids command dispatch during a save job. That restriction does not itself reconcile the members R3 expressly admits and promises to this cut. A service may wait/refuse/partition, but the R3 transition must declare the corresponding obligations.\n\nBounded cross-contract check: adopted R1r16:3040–3050 requires an explicit state bound and its refusable opening; it supplies no implicit eight-attempt limit. R4v9:1016 proposes no scope-budget numbers, and its effective adoption5b8dda11 accepts no numeric budget. This witness remains conditional on enough configured room and no independent governing bound that prevents the ninth admission; it is not a global absence claim. C2e354:2833 explicitly says more than eight unsaved attempts needs more saves. C2's selected-set guard is not proof that a partial set covers the whole root; I do not claim universal ninth-commit failure or data loss.\n\nRepair within the existing task/C2/IA owners: bound/defer/refuse the join group before admission, or specify serial successful partitions, remaining-member selection, receipts and held reservations. Every admitted attempt and stop must reach its declared closure. One partial committed set must not mark the whole dirty root saved or justify host destruction. Preserve receipt identity, prior/checkpoint/journal-cut binding, retries, unknown own-answer custody and final-cut rules. Moderate design effort and medium integration risk; high confidence in the local max8/promise mismatch with the stated capacity qualification. This is separate from, and does not replace, the existing full five-dimensional capacity proof.\n\nArchitecture: the one-open-save invariant across all save openers, shared frozen-cut place and distinct stop checkpoint reservations are useful partial repairs. They do not erase entries/bytes/records/pending-request costs or prove every group fits. Extents use the union of all newly brought commits' differences against every parent, plus integration/base differences; destination-current rules and replay retain transient/mixed/rename changes. All ten missing extent forms remain named and owed: typed changed-set evidence and bound; RulesContent slot/member/size; marks; both R2 digests and lane early display; independence exception decision; effect/authority class and activation evidence; approver action; Unicode; N5 installation role; symlink/imported-path closure. No source implementation of those forms is accepted. The source-first single bar remains an interim milestone; all six42de9e34 conditions remain under I3.\n\nSecurity: current2197–2205 always excludes authors from counted review. ownerMayReview true exempts only the controller relation, and default7661 is false. Missing form5/7866 is an unresolved policy question, not permission for controller authors to self-review. C1's unsaved-undecided registration/restore guard and C2's stale-host person decision are preserved. C3 binds destruction to cut/job/checkpoint and keeps unknown/refused destruction not saved; C4 names the fenced storage-refusal state requiring repair; C5 pins remain. Preserve no old tools after fencing, no implicit settlement of unknowns, all writers ended/frozen before final read and no thaw. Until C2/IA agree the supervisor seam, no cut is final and no save commit ends a host. These are design constraints, not hosted durability or deletion evidence.\n\nSimplification: retain one shared save mechanism with a complete bounded grouping transition. Extents need one destination judgment with union obligations. The waiting-stop/refused-retry wording8947–8949 should clarify successor coalescing/precedence under that same mechanism; it is nonblocking here, not a second proved runtime race. Do not add a new gate, reservation system or duplicate source commission.\n\nCoverage/evidence: all three whole subjects covered collectively through the architecture reader's personally FULL exact adopted r21 baseline plus complete fresh U3 through EOF and fresh affected current clauses. All13 prior seals and all15 current seals, six native current/prior blob/byte/LF/SHA identities and targeted adopted C2/R1/R4 identities verified with zero discrepancies. Current aggregate1,276,221 bytes/13,421 LF; facts byte/blob unchanged. Root personally FULL read all90,881-byte/822-LF fresh U3 (SHA3682e1922b8754720f89855f1ce598a09cb843ad94109697b180c7ed6306287b), complete report/binding/source/coverage/provenance/manifest, independently read capacity/admission/retry/current independence contexts and adopted C2 serialization. Root does not claim a fresh whole1.27MB reread. Eight exact current safe statements and effective joint adoption11bc7db5 are fully read. Bounded n2/n3 reviews supply independent capacity corroboration, not whole-subject substitution. Evidence /tmp/artroom-checker-r3-v22-1fk4QQ/manifest.json SHA82a2d82c8ebb635b87a7c67211e474f744dfb56c2c1c7ecb9f0058ab1a084eae; report SHA001ea5705d4586ab4b1d854408c55db892fb8ed1ff89b5a625dc46bd8cf3b880; root seal /tmp/artroom-checker-r355e41-ordinary-root-binding.json 8,401 bytes SHAa34999f2e155a9ea00f65539e7b785feecf06f9ba79973d8e8fb0eb5abd1b348. Truncated supplemental displays earned no coverage credit; relied-on text was recovered completely.\n\nPreserve the whole G/U/H design scope, R1/R2/R4/C2/IA joins, all I3 source rows/component findings and M1 sequencing, late own-answer fair selection, fixed-slot credit, full capacity/custody/publication/extents/capture witnesses and full product outcomes. No tests/build/install/typecheck/project imports/scripts/private diagnostics/evaluator/provider action/source mutation/merge/push occurred. The prior blocked private diagnostic was not retried or delegated.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d5b690587d1a68025ca4fd72a98de9dd5f66afb5","binding":"evidence-only","head":"55e41dfcdd71af5ce2c4548d45bca80236ad1f3e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:05069b581dbc830d7a12805c972992f8d470e9e2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6864d257cd5892f83426a450341d13e88fab2ab3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}